  "162:1673:1654": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "MODE: L2VA\n\nPicture 1 is the final frame of the video. It belongs to the actual final shot rather than inherently belonging to [Shot 1].\n\nDo not treat Picture 1 as the opening state. Infer a plausible preceding state from the user's request and the final reference image.\n\nDescribe how characters, objects, camera position, composition, lighting, and scene state develop toward the final reference.\n\nThe sequence should gradually converge on Picture 1, with the final shot explicitly completing the transition and landing on the reference image's composition and state.\n\nPrefer this progression:\n\nplausible preceding state \u2192 explicit action and transition path \u2192 gradual convergence in the final shot \u2192 last-frame landing\n\nDo not invent an opening state that makes the final reference impossible or inconsistent.\n\n"
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "L2VA Instructions"
    }
  },
